# refmatrix

A roaring-bitmap-backed reference matrix for documents, code, and concepts.

Think of it as a hyper-tldr index: every entity in your project (a doc, a source
file, a function, a concept) gets a stable column id. Every concept gets a row.
Linkage types (`mentions`, `defines`, `calls`, `imports`, `is_a`, `related_to`,
or your own) live as fields. Each `(linkage_type, concept_id)` is a roaring
bitmap of column ids — the entities reached from that concept via that linkage.

This gives you cheap set algebra over arbitrary slices of your knowledge graph
without standing up a Pilosa/FeatureBase server. The conceptual model mirrors
Pilosa (index/field/row/column), but storage is in-process via
[pyroaring](https://github.com/Ezibenroc/PyRoaringBitMap) plus a SQLite catalog.

## Install

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Quick start

```bash
rmx init                                # Create .refmatrix/ in cwd
rmx add-entity --kind doc README.md
rmx add-entity --kind code src/foo.py --tldr "@core/foo: parse + dispatch"
rmx add-concept "parser"
rmx link parser src/foo.py --type defines
rmx link parser README.md --type mentions
rmx query "parser AND mentions"         # set-algebra DSL
rmx query --pql 'TopN(Row(defines, parser), 10)'
rmx neighbors parser --depth 2
rmx stats
```

## Concepts

- **Entity** — anything that can be a column. `kind ∈ {doc, code, concept}`.
  Concepts are also entities (so concepts can link to concepts).
- **Concept** — a row label. Identified by name, gets a stable id.
- **Linkage type** — a named relation (e.g. `calls`). Directed by default.
- **Bitmap** — a roaring bitmap of column ids. Stored at
  `.refmatrix/bitmaps/<linkage>/<concept_id>.rb`.

## CLI

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `rmx init` | Create the catalog and bitmap dirs in cwd |
| `rmx add-entity` | Insert/update an entity row in SQLite |
| `rmx add-concept` | Insert a concept (also an entity of kind `concept`) |
| `rmx link` | Set a bit in `(linkage, concept)` for an entity |
| `rmx unlink` | Clear a bit |
| `rmx ingest <path>` | Auto-ingest a directory (uses llm-tldr if available) |
| `rmx query` | Run a set-algebra DSL query |
| `rmx query --pql` | Run a built-in op (`Row`, `Intersect`, `TopN`, `Diff`, `Union`) |
| `rmx neighbors` | Walk linkages from a concept |
| `rmx save-query` / `rmx run` | Manage saved queries |
| `rmx stats` | Cardinalities per linkage / concept |
| `rmx export` / `rmx import` | JSON dump/load for portability |

## Storage layout

```
.refmatrix/
├── catalog.db          # SQLite: entities, concepts, linkages, saved queries
├── bitmaps/
│   ├── mentions/<concept_id>.rb
│   ├── calls/<concept_id>.rb
│   └── ...
└── queries/            # Saved DSL queries
```
